WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.053
Misrepresentation is giving a false or misleading account of a policy:

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:09.646
its benefits, exclusions, premiums, dividends or the insurer’s financial condition.

00:00:09.646 --> 00:00:15.618
False advertising is the same deception in a brochure, website, seminar or ad.

00:00:15.618 --> 00:00:20.671
Telling Priya that a plan covers all prescriptions when it has

00:00:20.671 --> 00:00:25.723
a formulary, or calling a hospital indemnity policy health insurance, misrepresents.

00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:31.236
Omitting a material limitation can mislead as surely as a false statement.

00:00:31.236 --> 00:00:34.910
Maryland treats both as unfair trade practices under

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.585
Section 27-202, with penalties, restitution and license discipline.

00:00:38.585 --> 00:00:44.097
The cure is the same standard from Lesson 10: say what the

00:00:44.097 --> 00:00:49.150
policy does, what it does not, and who stands behind it.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.708
Competition is lawful; lying about competitors is not.

00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:58.491
Defamation under Section 27-204 is making or circulating a false or maliciously critical

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:04.273
statement about an insurer’s financial condition that is calculated to injure its business.

00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:09.166
Theo may point out that a rival plan has a narrower

00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:14.059
network; he may not claim the rival is insolvent without basis.

00:01:14.059 --> 00:01:19.841
Section 27-205 prohibits knowingly false statements about an insurer’s financial condition and false

00:01:19.841 --> 00:01:25.624
or deceptive entries in insurer records, including altering records to mislead an examiner.

00:01:25.624 --> 00:01:29.627
Fabricating a client’s signature on an application or backdating

00:01:29.627 --> 00:01:33.630
a receipt falls here as well as under fraud.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:39.776
A rebate is anything of value given to induce a purchase that

00:01:39.776 --> 00:01:45.921
is not specified in the policy: returning part of the commission, paying

00:01:45.921 --> 00:01:51.043
the first premium, giving a gift card after the sale.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:54.115
Section 27-209 prohibits rebating and inducements.

00:01:54.115 --> 00:02:00.261
Maryland allows educational materials, promotional materials and merchandise costing no more than

00:02:00.261 --> 00:02:05.895
50 dollars, but receipt may not be conditioned on buying insurance.

00:02:05.895 --> 00:02:12.040
A 20 dollar notebook handed to everyone at a seminar is lawful;

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:18.186
the same notebook promised only to those who enroll is a rebate.

00:02:18.186 --> 00:02:22.283
Both parts of the exception, the dollar limit

00:02:22.283 --> 00:02:25.868
and the no-condition rule, must be met.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:29.965
Rebating is a violation for the producer and

00:02:29.965 --> 00:02:33.550
for a client who knowingly accepts it.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:37.966
Twisting is inducing a policyholder to lapse, surrender, replace, convert

00:02:37.966 --> 00:02:42.382
or retain a policy through misrepresentation or an incomplete comparison.

00:02:42.382 --> 00:02:48.122
Section 27-213 covers retention as well as replacement: telling Rosa her current insurer

00:02:48.122 --> 00:02:53.863
is failing to make her switch is twisting, and so is falsely telling

00:02:53.863 --> 00:02:58.720
her the new plan is worse to keep her from switching.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.253
An honest, complete comparison that leads to a

00:03:02.253 --> 00:03:05.344
replacement is lawful, as Lesson 14 explained.

00:03:05.344 --> 00:03:11.085
The difference lies in the accuracy and completeness of what the producer says.

00:03:11.085 --> 00:03:14.617
Medigap and long-term care replacement rules add their

00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:18.150
own notices on top of the general prohibition.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.490
Paying someone for referrals is lawful only within limits.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:26.314
A fee to a person who does not sell, solicit or negotiate may

00:03:26.314 --> 00:03:31.139
be paid only if it is not conditioned on a sale and does

00:03:31.139 --> 00:03:35.963
not operate as a rebate to the buyer; a payment that depends on

00:03:35.963 --> 00:03:40.045
the referred customer buying is commission sharing with an unlicensed person.

00:03:40.045 --> 00:03:44.498
Describing active sales work as a referral does not change its nature.

00:03:44.498 --> 00:03:49.322
Maryland also prohibits boycott, coercion and intimidation: agreeing with others to refuse to

00:03:49.322 --> 00:03:54.147
deal with an insurer, or pressuring a lender’s customers to buy insurance through

00:03:54.147 --> 00:03:58.600
a particular producer as a condition of credit, are unfair trade practices.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:03.645
When a question describes conduct, match it to the practice.

00:04:03.645 --> 00:04:09.194
A false statement about a policy to make a sale: misrepresentation.

00:04:09.194 --> 00:04:13.230
The same statement in a mailer: false advertising.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.770
A false claim that an insurer is broke: defamation.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:21.806
A forged signature or altered record: false entry.

00:04:21.806 --> 00:04:25.842
Cash or a gift tied to buying: rebating.

00:04:25.842 --> 00:04:30.887
A misleading comparison to move or keep a policyholder: twisting.

00:04:30.887 --> 00:04:35.427
A payment to an unlicensed friend that depends on

00:04:35.427 --> 00:04:39.967
the sale: unlawful commission sharing dressed as a referral.

00:04:39.967 --> 00:04:47.030
Each carries administrative penalties, restitution and possible license action, and several are also crimes.
